WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.969
-Our first guest tonight is an
Emmy- and Golden Globe-nominated

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.471
actress for her role
as Piper Chapman

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.240
on Netflix's
"Orange is the New Black."

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.142
You can see her next in the
anthology series "Monsterland"

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:12.245
premiering October 2nd on Hulu.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.446
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:17.416
-Now, I am going to get
a white dove orchid,

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:20.553
and I'm going to keep that bitch
alive, so help me God.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.121
-Okay, gauntlet thrown.

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.455
-And I'm gonna
finish the scrapbook

00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:25.357
in time for Heather's
bat mitzvah. What else?

00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:26.559
-Yes, ma'am.
-What else?

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:30.263
Oh, I was thinking,
maybe I could kill Barb.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:31.297
I slash we.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.366
-Barb Bresler?
-No, Streisand.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.968
Yes, Barb Bresler,
wicked witch of the cul-de-sac.

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:38.304
-Murder Barb?

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.538
-Or maybe just her dog.

00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:41.440
You know, I'd settle
for her little dog.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.876
Susan.
-Susan.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.378
-Do you know that thing has
10,000 followers on Instagram?

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.414
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Taylor Schilling.

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:51.016
Hello, Taylor.
It's so good to see you.

00:00:51.016 --> 00:00:53.553
-Seth, it's so nice to see you.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.687
How are you?

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.555
-I'm hanging in there.
How about you?

00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:57.724
-Are ya?

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.425
Well, I feel better
now that I'm with you,

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.293
and I put on this fancy shirt.

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:02.995
-It's such a fancy shirt.

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:05.131
You know, there's always a fear
that people aren't gonna take it

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.567
seriously because they're
Zooming, and look at you.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.469
-No, I took it -- I haven't --

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.737
This is the most fancy
I've been in seven months.

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:14.206
I thought it was appropriate
to dress for Seth.

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:16.976
-And you really have,
and I feel like that plant,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.511
that's obviously
an A-plus plant.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.045
I don't want to overlook that.

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:22.715
-I cleared a surface.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:26.352
-It's just -- The whole thing
is just stunning, as always.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.887
-Isn't it a beautiful color?
-So thank you for being here.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.190
-Thank you. Thank you so much.
-How are you?

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.523
These are rough times
for everybody.

00:01:31.523 --> 00:01:34.060
Have you discovered
any new coping mechanisms?

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.296
-You know, Seth,
I think I've become

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:38.264
like a bit of
a narcoleptic person.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.565
-Oh, interesting.

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:43.269
-Like, I hear, like,
"Oh, plague and pestilence."

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.004
And then I go...
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.273
-Like, I pass out again.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.808
-Like, I just sleep,

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:51.710
or I'll fall asleep in different
areas, in new places.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.379
It's uncomfortable.
-That's interesting.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.848
So you just think you have,
like, an internal kill switch

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:58.584
that is just trying
to help you opt out of

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.319
the more stressful moments
that are happening right now?

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:02.388
-That's the only way
I can explain it

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.690
to myself and to my loved ones.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.258
-And is there ever like --

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:07.693
like, how do you know
this is happening?

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:09.061
Do you just,
all of sudden, wake up

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:10.497
and realize
that time has passed?

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.364
-There's been
photographic evidence.

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:14.967
Now, because I love you so much

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.602
and I love everyone here
so much,

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:19.405
I thought about
sharing a photo with you.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.007
-Right.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.942
-And then I shared it
with your producer,

00:02:23.942 --> 00:02:27.079
and we decided together
it would scare America...

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:28.714
-Yeah.
-...if I shared it publicly.

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:32.084
-The last thing we need
right now is to see you,

00:02:32.084 --> 00:02:36.089
one of America's many
sweethearts, in a situation

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.356
that would
bring more trouble in.

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:39.825
-A dark place.
I was ready to share it.

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:42.795
I was ready to offer it,
but it's dark.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.931
-I want to talk about the show,
but I also --

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.399
You mentioned a dog in the clip,
which makes me --

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:50.403
We've talked about it before,
but your dog, Tank --

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.571
How is Tank doing?

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:54.207
-You know, Tank is a light.
-Yeah.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.609
-Tank is hanging in there.
Tank's doing a great job.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:59.278
Tank is -- Tank's as steady
as she's ever been.

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:02.214
-I'm so happy to hear that,
and I want to show something

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:05.617
we've shown on the show before,
but I feel like it's something

00:03:05.617 --> 00:03:08.187
everyone needs to see again,
especially because

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:11.256
we're just looking for anything,
any little piece of joy

00:03:11.256 --> 00:03:13.059
that we can grab on to.
-Yeah.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:19.899
-You have a video of a time, you
argue, Tank said, "I love you."

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:22.101
-I mean, the proof
is in the pudding.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.670
We've been here before.
But we can revisit it.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:25.672
-Let's take a look.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.674
Here's Tank saying "I love you."

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.808
[ Tank squeals ]

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:33.846
-I love you. I love you.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.648
[ Tank squeals ]
[ Laughs ]

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:36.883
-There you go.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.818
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.120
-It doesn't get old, does it?

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.655
-No, it really doesn't get old.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:45.991
And you keep thinking
it's not going to happen.

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:49.662
And I just think it speaks
to how much Tank loves you

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.763
because it doesn't look like
it's easy for her to say it.

00:03:51.763 --> 00:03:53.232
-She's struggling.
She's suffering.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.334
-Like, it seems like it might
take a lot of physical effort.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:56.769
-She's struggling
and she's suffering

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.170
when she tries to say
"I love you."

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.672
It's not easy for her.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.874
-I know we've also -- you've
talked about trying to get

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:06.045
more dialogue, more ADR,
from Tank over the years.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:10.049
Have you had any success, or is
that the last thing Tank said?

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.717
-We're working on it.
-Yeah.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:17.022
-She really -- I -- We've tried
and I guess we've failed.

00:04:17.022 --> 00:04:18.524
-I mean, if you're gonna say
one thing --

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.525
-That's all I have to say.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:20.693
-If you're gonna say
one thing...

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:21.761
-We failed.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:22.562
-..."I love you" is the thing,
right?

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:23.528
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:23.528 --> 00:04:25.531
-Is Tank with you now?

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:28.434
-Are you ready?
-Yeah.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.169
-Come here!

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.571
Come here, girl. Come here.

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:34.273
Lookit!

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:36.342
-Oh, my God, see this?

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:39.779
There is some upside to doing
Zoom interviews on talk shows.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:43.382
-There is!
-Hi. Oh, my gosh, hi, Tank.

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:45.451
This is your moment.

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.086
This is your moment, Tank.

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:49.388
Tank, I just want to say
on behalf of all our viewers,

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:50.956
we love you.

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:52.825
-Tank, did you hear that?

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.327
She can't hear it.
She's trying so hard to breathe.

00:04:55.327 --> 00:04:56.495
She doesn't really have a nose.

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:58.064
It takes up all of her energy

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.566
just trying to get
the air in and out.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:04.570
-So that might really be one of
the reasons she's not talking

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.472
more often if she just, in
general, has trouble breathing.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.274
-Having trouble breathing.
-Yeah.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:09.741
-Oh, God.

00:05:09.741 --> 00:05:11.477
-Thank you for the cameo, Tank.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.714
And when we come back, we're
gonna talk more about your show.

